# Copied to `.env`, this is read by every build: `pnpm build` (next build), `pnpm build:vinext`
# (vite build) and the Cloudflare scripts (`pnpm build:cloudflare`, `pnpm deploy:cloudflare`).
# Only `next start` reads SITE_URL and SCVAL_BUILD_AT again at run time, so give it the same values
# as `next build`: the prerendered HTML has them baked in. The two vinext builds inline both into
# the server code (vite.config.ts), so `vinext start` and the Worker need neither.
#
# The Cloudflare scripts run in Vite mode `cloudflare`, so they load .env, .env.local,
# .env.cloudflare and .env.cloudflare.local, never .env.production: put the Worker build's own
# values (its SITE_URL) in .env.cloudflare.

# The site's own origin. It drives `metadataBase`, every `<link rel="canonical">`, the absolute
# URLs in sitemap.xml, the `Host`/`Sitemap` lines in robots.txt and the OG image URLs. For the
# Worker, its public origin: https://scvalfh.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev or a custom domain.
#
# There is no production domain in the repo, so the fallback is localhost (see
# components/layout/site-url.ts): set this in the deploy environment BEFORE the first production
# build or the shipped HTML will point at http://localhost:3000. No trailing slash.
SITE_URL=https://example.com

# Optional, CI only: pins the instant the "stale snapshot" notice is measured against
# (components/layout/build-instant.ts), so two builds of one commit are byte-identical.
# SCVAL_BUILD_AT=2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z

# Optional, Node only: read the snapshot (lib/data.ts) or the 2025-26 history (lib/history.ts)
# from another file instead of the copy every build bundles from data/. They are read with node:fs
# when the module loads, so they work for next and vinext's Node target, never on a Worker: leave
# them unset for the Cloudflare scripts and never make them Worker vars.
# SCVAL_SNAPSHOT=/absolute/path/to/snapshot.json
# SCVAL_HISTORY=/absolute/path/to/history-2025-26.json
